  "question": {
    "text": "If pH of a saturated solution of <math><mtext>Ba</mtext><msub><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mtext>OH</mtext></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is <math><mn>12</mn><mo>,</mo></math> the value of its <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtext>sp</mtext><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub></math> is found to be <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math> find the value of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">‘</mi><mi>n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">’</mi></math> here?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "As <math><mtext>pH</mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext>12</mtext></math><br /><math><mtext>pOH</mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext>14</mtext><mo>-</mo><mtext>12</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br /><math><mo>[</mo><mtext>OH</mtext><mo>]</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0</mn><mtext>1M</mtext><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math><br />In case of <math><munder><mrow><mtext>Ba</mtext><mo>(</mo><mtext>OH</mtext><msub><mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⇌</mo><munder><mrow><mtext>B</mtext><msup><mrow><mtext>a</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><mrow><mtext>2O</mtext><msup><mrow><mtext>H</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow></munder></math><br />As <math><mtext>2s</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0</mn><mtext>1</mtext><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mrow></mrow></math><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mrow></mrow></math><br />Ksp for <math><mtext>Ba</mtext><msub><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mtext>OH</mtext></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext>4</mtext><msup><mrow><mtext>s</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math><br />Hence <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">‘</mi><mi>n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">’</mi></math> = 5",
